<Ui xmlns="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/
..\FrameXML\UI.xsd">

    <!-- Vendored, not `externals:` in `.pkgmeta`. An external is only fetched by the packager, so
         the working tree would not have these files and neither the headless specs (`tests/run.js`
         loads real source under fengari) nor a locally-copied build would see them.

         LibStub is not loaded here. Debind loads it and Debind is a hard dependency, so it is
         already up by the time this addon is opened. Loading a second copy would be harmless but
         it would also be the only reason this addon needed Debind's Libs folder at all. -->
    <Script file="Libs\LibDeflate\LibDeflate.lua"/>

    <!-- LibSerialize v1.2.2 (MINOR 6), taken 2026-08-14 after a pin that held it at v1.2.1.

         The pin is recorded because the thing that caused it can come back: v1.2.2's negative-zero
         check opens with `if num == 0 and 1 / num < 0`, which every number write passes through,
         and one `_ptr_` build raised "Division by zero" on that rather than answering `inf`. Every
         payload we build is full of zeros (`spec = 0` on each account-wide layer, any zeroed
         condition mask), so on that build v1.2.2 could not export at all - and that client is
         where this gets tested. It answers `inf` now.

         So if export starts erroring on a client that used to work, this line is the suspect, and
         reverting to v1.2.1 is the workaround rather than a fix.

         `devdocs/building-export-import.md` has the measurements and the cross-version read. -->
    <Script file="Libs\LibSerialize\LibSerialize.lua"/>

</Ui>
